quran[27]{c,v,t}:
  55,68,"In both of them, there will be fruits, date palms and pomegranates."
  55,69,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
  55,70,"In them (all), there will be good-natured and beautiful (chaste maidens)."
  55,71,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
  55,72,"Wide-eyed maidens, secluded in pavilions."
  55,73,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
  55,74,"Whom no human has ever touched before, nor jinn."
  55,75,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
  55,76,Reclining upon green cushions and magnificent carpets.
  55,77,Then which of your Lord’s blessings do you both deny?
  55,78,Blessed is the Name of your Lord—the Possessor of Majesty and Honour.
  56,1,"When the Inevitable Event takes place,"
  56,2,none shall deny its occurrence.
  56,3,"(It will be) debasing (for the disbelievers), elevating (for the believers)."
  56,4,"When the earth is shaken violently,"
  56,5,"and the mountains are crushed to pieces,"
  56,6,"and they become scattered (particles of) dust,"
  56,7,you will be (divided) into three groups:
  56,8,"The People of the Right Hand, how (happy) are the People of the Right Hand!"
  56,9,"And the People of the Left Hand, how (miserable) are the People of the Left Hand!"
  56,10,And the Foremost (in faith) will be the Foremost (in Paradise).
  56,11,"Those are the ones brought near (to Allah),"
  56,12,(who will reside) in the Gardens of Bliss.
  56,13,"Many (of them are) from the earlier generations,"
  56,14,and a few from the later generations.
  56,15,"(They will be) upon couches brocaded with golden embroidery,"
  56,16,reclining on them facing one another.
